<li>Why money is not allowed for monks?
                            <ul>
<li>money is very <b>desirable</b> </li>
<li>"if money was allowed for bhikkhus all sense pleasures would be allowed."</li>
<li>The Buddha allows bhikkhus to even go to the extent of collecting grains, bread, and so on for travelling, but in no instance money is allowed.</li>
<li>When bhikkhus have needs the laity may not be able to provide them and when the laity is able to provide them the bhikkhus may not have any needs therefore the Buddha allowed proper ways through which bhikkhus can receive allowable things.</li>
